                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{lcpt,proper}
                  for the category of Hausdorff and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
                  with morphisms being the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
                  of topological spaces.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Top
                          %mrow
                            %mi lcpt
                            %mo ,
                            %mi inf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{lcpt,inf}
                  for the category of Hausdorff and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
                  with morphisms being the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
                  that vanish at infinity.
          %p
            The duality itself is exhibited by the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          #FunctorsOfFunctionAlgebras.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi com
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \;\colon\; Top_{cpt} \to C^\ast Alg_{com}^{op}
            %p
              for the functor which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the algebra of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi continuous
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X) = \{f : X \to \mathbb{C} | f \; continuous\}
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_0 \;\colon\; */Top_{cpt} \to C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}^{op}
            %p
              for the functor that sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x_0)
              to the algebra of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to \mathbb{C}
              for which
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_0) = 0
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sp
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi com
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sp : C^\ast Alg_{com}^{op} \to Top_{cpt}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+spectrum"} Gelfand spectrum
              functor: it sends a commutative
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to the set of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/character"}> character
                s
              – non-vanishing
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x : A \to \mathbb{C}
              – equipped with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+topology"} spectral topology
            %p Similarly write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sp
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi lcpt
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sp : C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}^{op} \to Top_{lcpt}
                    \\,.
          %h2#statement Statement
          #GelfandDualityTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Unital Gelfand duality theorem)
            %p The pair of functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi com
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi sp
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg_{com}^{op} \stackrel{\overset{C}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{sp}{\to}} Top_{cpt}
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg^{op}_{\cdots}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg_{\cdots}
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              On non-unital
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi sp
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mn 0
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}^{op} \stackrel{\overset{C_0}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{sp}{\to}} */Top_{cpt}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The operation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitalization"} unitalization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+
              constitutes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi nu
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi ker
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg_{nu}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{(-)^+}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{ker}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    C^\ast Alg / \mathbb{C}
            %p
              between non-unital
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over-category"} over-category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %p
              Composed with the equivalence of theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GelfandDualityTheorem"}
              this yields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                      %mi op
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi com
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi C
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}^{op}
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{(-)^+}{\to}
                    (C^\ast Alg_{com}/\mathbb{C})^{op}
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{C}{\to}
                    * / Top_{cpt}
                    \\,.
            %p The weak inverse of this is the composite functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi cpt
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi com
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ker
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_0 : */Top_{cpt}
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{sp}{\to}
                    (C^\ast Alg_{com}/\mathbb{C})^{op}
                    \\underoverset{\simeq}{ker}{\to}
                    C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}^{op}
            %p
              which sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (* \stackrel{x_0}{\to} X)
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ev
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi x
                                %mn 0
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(C(X) \stackrel{ev_{x_0}}{\to} \mathbb{C})
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f \in C(X) | f(x_0) = 0\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FunctorsOfFunctionAlgebras"}
          #ForLocallyCompactTopologicalSpaces.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+Hausdorff+spaces+are+equivalently+open+subspaces+of+compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} locally compact Hausdorff spaces are equivalently open subspaces of compact Hausdorff spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              on the compact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\ast
              which vanishes at the extra point is equivalently a continuous function on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              which
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishes at infinity
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi lcpt
                        %mo ,
                        %mi inf
                    %mo ⇆
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{lcpt,inf} \leftrightarrows C^\ast Alg_{com,nu}
            %p between the category of locally compact Hausdorff spaces and continuous maps vanishing at infinity and the category of commutative nonunital C*-algebras.
            %p
              The duality also works with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              instead of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              (
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone82"}> Johnstone 82, chapter IV
              )
            %p
              For an overview of other generalizations see also
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/82960/381"} this MO discussion
          %p
            If one uses nondegenerate morphisms of C*-algebras instead, the duality works for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Brandenburg07"} Brandenburg 07
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi lcpt
                        %mo ,
                        %mi proper
                    %mo ⇆
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mrow
                        %mi com
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nu
                        %mo ,
                        %mi nd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{lcpt,proper} \leftrightarrows C^\ast Alg_{com,nu,nd}
            %p
              between the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact"} locally compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+spaces"} Hausdorff spaces
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"} proper maps
              and the category of commutative nonunital
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
              with nondegenerate *-homomorphisms as morphisms.
          %h2#generalizations Generalizations
          %h3#in_constructive_mathematics In constructive mathematics
          %p
            Gelfand duality makes sense in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to any
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+Gelfand+duality+theorem"} constructive Gelfand duality theorem
          %h3#by_horizontal_categorification By horizontal categorification
          %p
            Gelfand duality can be extended by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+categorification"} horizontal categorification
            to define the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaceoid"} spaceoids
            as formal duals of commutative
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star-category"} categories
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
